{
  "name": "draw-from-element-fan-in",
  "category": "draw",
  "note": "Draw one element around Create_Support_Case, which thirteen elements lead into: twelve alike assignments (one per region and team) and a decision. Drawn one box each, the twelve would sit in one row and make the picture unreadably wide. The contract groups alike elements that lead straight in, so the picture stays small; the decision Check_Existing_Case is a different type and must keep its own box. Every API-looking name in the picture must exist in the flow. The picture must give the decision a node of its own (a label that starts with its name) and a group box that carries the count, so a picture that grouped the decision in, or drew no group at all, fails.",
